    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d479">

                <pb facs="0527" n="515" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg515"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710. Consultation 3/489: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-01-26T20:00:00-04:00">January 26, 1942—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>40. Following telegram has been sent to the Embassy, Rio de Janeiro.</p>
                <p>“January 26, 8 p.m. For the Under Secretary.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d479-f1"/> Your
                    January 24, 5 p.m. Acting Minister for Foreign Affairs<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d479-f2"/> this afternoon showed me telegram sent yesterday to
                    Bolivian Minister for Foreign Affairs<anchor n="3" xml:id="d479-f3"/> in Rio de
                    Janeiro authorizing him to announce that Bolivian Government confirmed its
                    intention to break off relations with Axis Powers. Telegram went on to tell Anze
                    he should secure following commitments from you as preliminary to issuance of
                    decree enacting rupture used [<hi rendition="#italic">sic</hi>].</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Guarantee that United States would protect Bolivia from aggression by Axis
                        Powers against the ‘other nations’.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Increase in capital of Bolivian Development Corporation<anchor n="4"
                            xml:id="d479-f4"/> to ‘at least $40,000,000’.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Increase in prices for Bolivian minerals sold to Metals Reserve and
                        substitution of f.o.b. Chilean ports for c.i.f. United States ports in tin
                            contract.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d479-f5"/></item>
                </list>
                <p>Acting Minister for Foreign Affairs stated to me that actual breach would take
                    place within 2 or 3 days if these conditions were met. It seems obvious that
                    Anze exceeded instructions in his speech at Plenary session announcing rupture
                    …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>I have an interview with the President<anchor n="6" xml:id="d479-f6"/> at 11 a.m.
                    tomorrow at which I shall endeavor to present matters in such a light as to
                    secure <pb facs="0528" n="516" xml:id="pg516"/> immediate issuance of decree
                    breaking relations. Will submit full report thereafter.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Department as my 40, January 26, 8 p.m.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d479-f1" n="1" xml:id="d479-f1-content">
                <p>Sumner Welles was representing the United States at the Third Meeting of the
                    Foreign Ministers of the American Republics at Rio de Janeiro, January 15–28,
                    1942; for correspondence on this Meeting, see <ref target="#pg6">pp. 6</ref>
                    ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d479-f2" n="2" xml:id="d479-f2-content">
                <p>Justo Rodas Eguino.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d479-f3" n="3" xml:id="d479-f3-content">
                <p>Eduardo Anze Matienzo.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d479-f4" n="4" xml:id="d479-f4-content">
                <p>For correspondence concerning this Corporation, see section entitled “Program for
                    economic cooperation between the United States and Bolivia”, <ref
                        target="#pg592">pp. 592</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d479-f5" n="5" xml:id="d479-f5-content">
                <p>See <ref target="frus1940v05#pg_524"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, 1940, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">v</hi>, pp.
                        524</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d479-f6" n="6" xml:id="d479-f6-content">
                <p>Gen. Enrique Peñaranda y del Castillo.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
